# Brave Harness (bh / bh-multi) — default browser for all agents

**Canonical file. Edit here; all agent runtimes inherit via their mirrors.**

Any agent (Claude Code, Grok Build, Codex, Cursor, opencode, Gemini, Aider, Cline) that needs a real browser uses the **Brave harness**, NOT Playwright / Puppeteer / Selenium / Chrome-for-Testing.

Installed and on PATH. Do not `npm install playwright`. Do not re-smoke-test the harness each session. Just use it.

## HARD DEFAULT: compact native interface first

Use `bhn` for normal browser reads, actions, console checks, and network checks:

```bash
bhn qa state
bhn qa click e3
bhn qa fill e4 "text"
bhn qa observe
```

`bhn` is a structured companion over the existing `bh-multi` and Browser Harness
session. It returns compact JSON, reusable element refs, state deltas, and filtered
errors. It never takes screenshots or emits cookies, request headers, URL query values,
or input values.

Use BrowserCode for arbitrary CDP code or reusable scripts:

```bash
bcx qa eval 'return document.title'
bcx qa run .bcode/agent-workspace/task.js
```

`bcx` calls BrowserCode's `browser_execute` directly against the chosen `bh-multi`
profile without invoking BrowserCode's LLM. It is a shared lane for Claude, Cursor, Pi,
OpenCode, Codex, and other agents.

Use raw `bh-multi run` only when neither `bhn` nor `bcx` fits. If the same inline script
is needed twice, add a `bhn` primitive or save a `bcx` script.

---

## HARD DEFAULT: native data, not screenshots

**Do not take screenshots unless the user explicitly asks.**

Treat the page as structured data (text, roles, buttons, inputs, forms), not pixels.

| Need | How |
|------|-----|
| URL / title / viewport | `page_info()` |
| Page text, buttons, labels, forms | `js(...)` DOM reads |
| Click / type | `js` click by text/selector when possible; else `click_at_xy`, `type_text`, `press_key` |
| Tabs | `list_tabs`, `switch_tab`, `new_tab`, `goto_url` |
| Extensions | open `chrome://extensions` or extension pages; interact via `js` / CDP on those targets |
| Console / network | `drain_events()` |
| Nested apps (iframes) | `iframe_target(...)` then DOM reads |

### Screenshots (`capture_screenshot`)

**Off by default.** Only when the user explicitly asks, or a rare visual-only gate they requested.

Do **not** screenshot after every action, for "sanity checks," or as the primary way to find buttons.

---

## Two entry points

| CLI | Use |
|-----|-----|
| `bh` / `browser-harness` | Single default profile, quick one-offs |
| `bh-multi` | Isolated Brave profiles (own port, cookies, session). Prefer for QA and multi-account work |

Binaries: `~/.local/bin/bh-multi`, `browser-harness` (PATH).  
Brave: `/Applications/Brave Browser.app`. Profiles: `~/.bh-profiles/<name>/`.

### bh-multi commands

```bash
bh-multi launch <name>          # start isolated Brave + daemon
bh-multi run <name> "<script>"  # run harness DSL on that profile
bh-multi all "<script>"         # same script on every active profile
bh-multi list                   # active profiles + ports
bh-multi stop <name> | stop-all
bh-multi login <name> <url>     # optional credentials.json auto-fill
```

Default QA profile name: **`qa`**.

```bash
bh-multi launch qa   # once per machine session if stopped
bh-multi run qa "goto_url('https://example.com'); wait_for_load(); print(page_info())"
```

---

## HARD RULE: preserve the named browser session

`bh-multi` profiles are persistent shared browser sessions, not disposable test processes.
A verification command finishing must NOT close Brave, its daemon, or the named profile.

Before launching:

```bash
bh-multi list
```

- If the named profile is already running, reuse it. Do not relaunch it.
- If it is stopped, run `bh-multi launch <name>` once, then confirm with `bh-multi list`.
- Use a stable, task-specific profile name. Continue every action with `bh-multi run <same-name> ...`.
- Leave the profile running when verification finishes. State which profile was left active.
- Only run `bh-multi stop <name>` or `bh-multi stop-all` when the user explicitly asks to close the browser session.

Hard lifecycle bans:

- Never add `bh-multi stop`, `stop-all`, `pkill`, `killall`, raw PID kills, or profile deletion as automatic cleanup.
- Never use an `EXIT`/`trap`/`finally` cleanup that stops Brave or the harness daemon.
- Never close or terminate the PTY/session that owns a foreground harness process while verification is ongoing.
- Keep the app dev server and browser harness in SEPARATE named PTY sessions. Stopping the dev server must not stop Brave.
- Do not combine harness launch, dev-server startup, verification, and cleanup into one shell pipeline.
- A shell command timeout is NOT permission to kill Brave or the harness. Poll the named session instead.

If Brave closes unexpectedly, relaunch the SAME profile name. Its cookies and local state
remain in `~/.bh-profiles/<name>/`. Do not create a replacement profile unless isolation
is intentionally required.

---

## Harness DSL

Python-flavored; statements separated by `;`. Always `print(...)` values you need on stdout.

| Call | Does |
|------|------|
| `goto_url('https://…')` | navigate (prefer `new_tab` for first nav if you must not clobber the active tab) |
| `new_tab()` / `new_tab('https://…')` | open tab |
| `wait_for_load()` / `wait(secs)` | await load / sleep |
| `page_info()` | `{url,title,w,h,sx,sy,pw,ph}` |
| `js('<expression>')` | eval JS in page; primary inspection tool |
| `click_at_xy(x, y)` | pixel click when DOM targeting fails |
| `type_text('…')` / `press_key('Enter')` | keyboard |
| `scroll(dx, dy)` | scroll |
| `drain_events()` | console + network buffer |
| `iframe_target(...)` | nested iframe context |
| `list_tabs()` / `switch_tab(...)` / `current_tab()` | tabs |
| `http_get(url)` | fetch from browser context |
| `ensure_real_tab()` | leave chrome:// / blank targets |
| `close_tab(tid)` / `reap_tabs()` | close one / close redundant (auto) |
| `cdp` | low-level CDP when needed |
| `capture_screenshot(path)` | **only if user asked** |

### Tab hygiene is automatic. Do not audit tabs.

Leftover tabs pile up until Brave hangs the machine, so `new_tab()` reaps them
itself. **Never list tabs "to check for cleanup", never close tabs proactively,
and never add a cleanup step to a browser task.** It is handled.

The reaper is silent below 8 tabs (`BH_MAX_TABS`, `0` disables) and only closes
**redundant** tabs: the driven tab survives, one copy of each URL survives,
blanks and `chrome://` go, and a page open exactly **once is never closed**.
It cannot take the last copy of anything.

Only touch this if the user asks, or a task genuinely needs many tabs of the
same URL open at once (then `reap_tabs(threshold=0)` or `BH_MAX_TABS=0`).

### Native inspection examples

```bash
# Page text
bh-multi run qa "print(js('document.body && document.body.innerText.slice(0,5000)'))"

# Buttons and links
bh-multi run qa "print(js(\"[...document.querySelectorAll('button,a,[role=button]')].map(e=>({t:(e.innerText||e.getAttribute('aria-label')||'').trim().slice(0,80), href:e.href||null})).filter(x=>x.t).slice(0,40)\"))"

# Click by visible label
bh-multi run qa "print(js(\"[...document.querySelectorAll('button')].find(b=>b.innerText.includes('Connect'))?.click(); 'clicked'\"))"
```

---

## Extensions

Agents **can** work with Brave extensions:

1. `goto_url('chrome://extensions')` or open the extension’s popup / options URL
2. `list_tabs()` to find the extension page target
3. `js(...)` / `cdp` on that tab for UI and state
4. Wallet / dapp: prefer `window.ethereum.request` via `js` when injected; use extension UI only when needed

Never assume Playwright-style extension APIs. Use real browser targets.

---

## Credentials / multi-account

- `~/.bh-profiles/credentials.json` (gitignored) → `bh-multi login <name> <url>`
- Cookie JSON rule: `~/.config/<service>/cookies.json` with `chmod 600` (global secret rule)
- Never paste passwords or cookies into prompts

---

## E2E gate recipe (native-first)

```bash
bh-multi launch qa
bh-multi run qa "goto_url('<URL>'); wait_for_load(); wait(1); print(page_info())"
bh-multi run qa "print(js('document.body.innerText.slice(0,3000)'))"
bh-multi run qa "print(drain_events())"   # fail on uncaught errors
# interact via js click / type_text
# optional: ph > h check via page_info for one-screen UIs
```

FAIL on: uncaught console errors, broken primary CTA, blank content, missing expected copy, dead API/CORS (verify with fetch/`http_get` where relevant).

